introduction :
--------------
Hi, I’m Srinivas, an SAP CPI Consultant with a strong background in software development.
I began my career working with Java, Kotlin, and Groovy, which gave me a solid foundation in
object-oriented programming, scripting, and backend logic. This development experience plays
a key role in my ability to build robust and flexible integration solutions.

I specialize in end-to-end iFlow development using SAP Cloud Platform Integration (CPI).
I’ve worked extensively with components like Content Modifier, Router, Aggregator, Splitter/Gather,
Join, Converters, Content Enrich, Poll Enrich, Request-Reply, Send, and Data Store operations.

I’m proficient in Groovy scripting, JSON and XSLT transformations, node functions, and graphical
message mapping. My integration designs often incorporate patterns such as routing, splitting,
enrichment, exception handling, and ProcessDirect, while also making use of Local Integration Processes
and Exception Subprocesses for modularity and reusability.

I regularly handle dynamic configurations and secure authentication methods, including OAuth,
Basic Authentication, and Client Certificates. My experience spans integration with systems
like S/4HANA and Concur, using a wide range of adapters such as JMS, SFTP, Advance Event mesh,
HTTP, SOAP, OData, IDoc, JDBC, Mail, RFC, and SuccessFactors adapters.

Beyond CPI, I have practical experience with SAP Event Mesh, build
event-driven integrations with third-party systems. I’ve worked with SAP API Management to design
and secure APIs with policies and whitelisting. I’ve also handled IDoc processing from S/4HANA,
configured ALE and RFC destinations, and used SAP Cloud Connector to enable secure connectivity
between cloud and on-premise systems. Additionally, I’ve used SAP Open Connectors to integrate
external SaaS platforms through unified APIs.

In my day-to-day role, I focus on designing, developing, and deploying integration flows,
promoting artifacts across landscapes using SAP TMS, and monitoring and troubleshooting
through CPI Monitor, logs, and trace tools. I actively participate in scrum meetings,
client discussions, and grooming sessions. I also ensure optimal performance by using
efficient filter and select queries in OData/HTTP calls, minimizing payload sizes,
and leveraging appropriate message exchange patterns. To support effective monitoring
and debugging, I implement strategic payload logging and custom trace points without
impacting system performance.

I’m passionate about building clean, scalable, and high-performing integrations with
robust exception handling and streamlined observability. I continuously stay updated
with the latest SAP




